@xuenay Have you considered working in ML engineering?
I know that you're interested in the field of AI, and I expect that the shortage of people with ML expertise will continue.
Your publication history could also help you get a job in ML if your fundamentals are strong too.

@kandouss Divesting should hurt them a little bit by effectively "competing with them".
More analysis here: https://t.co/ol5deIFAgZ
I think the most common limited-downside way of "divesting" from a single company would be to buy a long put on the company.

@RichardMCNgo I agree that the healthcare one was a bit weaker than the others, although people not being interested in surgeon outcome history is surprising. 

Others are politics, consumption, art and charity. 

"grey tribe" techies tend to more intelligence signaling vs virtue signaling.

