@michael_nielsen Slight correction, the model was shown only 100 examples of the task, not 10,000.
10,000 was the number of examples we used in the test set for calculating accuracy.
This doesn't change your argument though. The model was indeed bad at reversing words!

@KevinSimler "financial risk". I get that risk is related to the variance of an asset and that folks need a risk premium to hold risky assets, but things seem murky after that. 

How do we evaluate variance for these non-stationary distributions?

How much financial risk aversion is rational?

@christinahkim Most stuff will be popular papers if you’re doing the newsletter+twitter strategy. 

